# pocketbase/ — template only. Nothing here is ever filled in and committed.
#
# Local development needs none of these: `pnpm pb:dev` serves a scratch database
# with no email and no object storage. They exist so the shape is written down
# before T2/T4 need them, and so the hosted instance is configured from a list
# rather than from memory.

# Where the app is, so the guardian-consent email can link to it (T6). The
# links point at `/consent/approve/<token>` and `/consent/revoke/<token>` on the
# web app, never at the API.
#
# Leave it blank locally — it defaults to http://localhost:3000, which is what
# `pnpm dev` serves. On the hosted instance it is `https://landthetrick.com`,
# and getting it wrong sends a parent a link to their own machine.
LANDIT_APP_URL=

# Prints the guardian's two links to the server log when the email cannot be
# sent, so the consent flow can be walked through locally. **Off in production**:
# an approval link in a log is an approval link, and the rider it belongs to
# could use it on themselves. Any non-empty value turns it on.
LANDIT_CONSENT_DEBUG_LINKS=

# Transactional email over SMTP — auth, password reset, guardian consent.
# Which provider is a plan §1 decision, not a code one; nothing in the repo
# names it, and moving to another is these five values.
#
# **Nothing reads these.** They are the shape of what PocketBase needs, not an
# interface it offers: PocketBase takes its mail configuration from its settings
# database, entered in the admin UI at Settings → Mail and persisted in the
# `/pb_data` volume. Set them as environment variables on the hosted instance
# and you get a tidy variable list and an instance that still cannot send.
# Keep the list — it is what to have on screen when filling that form in — but
# fill the form, not the environment. See docs/infrastructure.md runbook 6.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
SMTP_SENDER_ADDRESS=
SMTP_SENDER_NAME=Land The Trick

# Clip storage: Cloudflare R2 through PocketBase's S3 backend. Private bucket;
# clips are delivered by short-lived file token only, never publicly.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_BUCKET=
S3_REGION=auto
S3_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_SECRET=
